==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Santa Kuu, type γ''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Santa Kuu fortunately got a better fate than [[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Kuu, type γ]]. The former has generally higher stats, which is a good sign, and more importantly, better trait targets. If obtained early, Santa Kuu can make prompt work of [[Into the Future]], especially the [[Floating Continent (Into the Future)|Floating Continent]] stages that contain enemies of both her target traits. Speaking of which, she does fine against them in general; Santa Kuu outranges a good portion of them, even [[Angelic Sleipnir|Angelic Slepnir]] by a slight margin, and her solid effective HP and DPS keep her alive for quite some time. Being a spinoff of Kuu, however, means that the player will be dealing with an exuberantly long attack frequency and inconvenient foreswing, potentially causing missed hits.

An even bigger issue is a lack of catching up to the original Kuu in terms of content. Modern Alien enemies now have plenty of tools at hand: [[Warp]], [[Barrier]]s, [[Long Distance]]/[[Wave Attack|Wave]] attacks, and generally a more menacing disposition—factors the [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] are able to counter but Santa Kuu is oblivious to. For Angels, many other Ubers are more up-to-date, stronger, and more reliable than her, from [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Deth-Troy-R]] to [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Moving Castle]], and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] has far more interesting perks while being a solid anti-Angel.

Divine Kuu γ even got [[Talents|Ultra Talents]] before Santa Kuu got her [[True Form]], with new, better niches and a cure for Divine Kuu γ's infamous attack frequency leaving Santa Kuu in the dust. This at least gives Santa Kuu plenty of room to improve in the future, but currently, she becomes an outdated collector's item once [[Cats of the Cosmos]] is cleared.

